Text typed into a new, empty paragraph and then made a link shows once, as the link. On a frontend that keeps its DOM between renders (React, Next.js), the typed text stayed in front of the link as plain text. The bridge kept asking the frontend to draw a zero-width space in the paragraph's first leaf after the author had typed there; once linking emptied that leaf again, the frontend was handed the same value it had drawn before and left the typed text in place. The bridge now forgets that caret target as soon as the author types into the field.
